    "title": {
      "en": "An Old Woman near Taizan"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Gathering and releasing � the stick is always with him; \nAble to kill and able to give life � the balance remains in his hands.  \nDelusive passions, devils and non-Buddhists � he controls them all at his finger tip; \nThe great earth, the mountains and rivers � all become his toys.  \nJust tell me, what sort of inner dimension is this?\n\nThere was an old woman on the way to Taizan.  Whenever a monk asked her how to get to Taizan, she would answer, �Go straight on.�  After the monk had gone a few steps, she would say, �This good and na�ve fellow goes off that way, too.�  \nLater a monk told J�sh� about this.  J�sh� said, �Wait a bit.  I will go and see through her for you.�  He went and asked the same question.\nThe next day, J�sh� ascended the rostrum and said, �I have seen through the old woman for you.�\n\nOld in age, he has become a spirit, making no mistakes in transmission;\nThe old buddha J�sh� succeeded to Nansen.\nThe old turtle loses its life because of the designs on its back;\nEven the �excellent four horses� and the �Wind Chaser� are encumbered by the bridle.\nThe �old woman's Zen� has been seen through:\nIf you preach it to people, it isn't worth a penny."
    },
