    "id": "shoyo_22",
    "title": {
      "en": "Gant�'s Bow to the Kaatzu"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Human beings are examined with words, water is checked with a stick.\nSweeping grasses and witnessing the wind � this is what is normally applied.\nWhat if all of a sudden a tiger with a burned tail springs out?\n\nGant� came to Tokusan.  He straddled the threshold of the gate and asked, �Is this ordinary or is this holy?�  Tokusan shouted, �Kaatzu!�  Gant� made a deep bow.\nHearing of this, T�zan said, �Hardly anyone but Gant� could have accepted it that way.�\nGant� said, �Old T�zan can't tell between good and bad.  At that time, I raised up with one hand and suppressed with the other.�\n\nFoiling the attempt of the on-comer, holding the gripe of authority;\nThings have rules after which they must be performed;\nNations have laws that must not be violated.\nThe guest reverently brings his gift, and the host becomes proud;\nThe lord dislikes admonition, and the subordinate flatters.\nWhat is the meaning of Gant�'s questioning Tokusan?\nOne raising, one suppressing � observe well his mind and action!"
    },
