    "id": "shoyo_37",
    "title": {
      "en": "Isan's �Karma-Consciousness�"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Driving the plowman�s ox and dragging his nose around; \nRobbing the hungry man of his food and grabbing his throat fast.  \nIs there anyone who can wield [such] a poisonous hand?\n\nIsan asked Ky�zan, �Suppose a man asks you, saying, 'All living beings are tossed in a vast karma-consciousness, and have no foundation to rely upon.'  How would you check him?�  Ky�zan said, �If such a monk appears, I call out to him, 'Mr. So-and-so!'  When he turns his head, instantly I say, 'What is this?'  If he hesitates, then I say to him, 'Not only is there a vast karma-consciousness, but also there is no foundation to rely upon.'�  Isan said, �Good.�\n\nOne calls you, and you turn your head around�do you know your self or not?\nThe full moon, shining vaguely through ivy, even becomes a crescent.\nThe child of great riches is ruined a bit;\nEndlessly destitute, how sorrowful the person is!"
    },
