    "text": {
      "en": "The pure ground without an inch of grass for ten thousand miles still deludes people;\nThe clear sky without a speck of could in eight directions still deceives you.\nEven if one removes a wedge by [driving in] another wedge, \nIt does not avoid sustaining emptiness by using emptiness.\nObserve well a special method � a hammer upon the back of the head!\n\nGreat Master Tokusan Emmy� instructed his assembly and said, �If you have exhausted to the end, you will realize right away that all buddhas in the three worlds have stuck their mouths to the wall.  Yet there is still one person, who is giving a great laugh.  If you can recognize that person, your Zen study has been accomplished.�\n\nGathering in � holding fast the throat:\nWinds polish, clouds wipe; the water is cool, the sky is autumn.\nNever say the brocade-scaled fish has no good taste:\nOne hook of the moon fishes out [the waters of] the S�r� River.."
