    "id": "shoyo_56",
    "title": {
      "en": "Misshi and the White Rabbit"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Even if you sank forever in hell, you would not look for the liberation of the saints; \nDaibadatta [=Devadatta] enjoyed the bliss of the three-Dhyana-Heaven \namid uninterrupted hell.\nUzuranbotsu [=Uddaka-Ramaputta] fell from the zenith of heaven \ndown into the body of a flying raccoon. \nJust tell me, where is the gain or loss?\n\nWhen Uncle Misshi and T�zan were walking together, they saw a white rabbit run by in front of them.   Misshi said, �How swift!�  T�zan said, �In what way?�  Misshi said, �It is just like a person in white clothes being venerated as a prime minister.�  T�zan said, �You are such an elderly and respectable man, and still you say something like that?�  Misshi said, �Then how about you?�  T�zan said, �A noble of an ancient house is temporarily fallen into poverty.�\n\nComparing the strength with snow and frost;\nWalking smoothly upon elevated clouds.\nKakei [=Xiahui] left his country;\nSh�jo [=Siangru] passed the bridge.\nSh�ka [=Xiao] and S�shin [=Caop]� s strategy established the Han Dynasty;\nThe body and mind of S�ho [=Caho] and Kyoy� [=Xu] wanted to evade Emperor Gy� [=Yao].\nPeople are disturbed by favor and disgrace � find deep faith in yourself.\nThe traces of the true heart get mingled and mixed with those of fishermen and woodcutters."
    },
