    "id": "shoyo_64",
    "title": {
      "en": "Shish�'s �Succession�"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Sh�y� intimately encountered Bokush�, yet he burnt succession incense for old Sepp�;\nT�su personally received it from Enkan, yet he succeeded in the Dharma to Daiy�.\nJade blossoms bloom upon the coral branches;\nGold fruit ripens in the forest of sandalswood.\nJust tell me, how do such creations take place?\n\nHead Monk Shish� asked H�gen, �You have opened a zendo, Master.  But who did you succeed to?�  H�gen said, �Master Jiz�.�  Shish� said, �You have gone a great deal against your late master Ch�kei.�  H�gen said, �I still don't understand a turning word of Ch�kei's.�  Shish� said, �Why didn't you ask me?�  H�gen said, �'The one body manifests itself in myriad phenomena' � what does it mean?�  Shish� stuck up his whisk.  H�gen said, �That is what you learned under Ch�kei.  What is your own view, Head Monk?�  Shish� was silent.  H�gen said, �When it is said, 'The one body manifests itself in myriad phenomena' � are the myriad phenomena swept away or are they not?�  Shish� said, �Not swept away.�  H�gen said, �There are two.�  All the disciples on the right and the left side said, �Swept away.�  H�gen said, �The one body manifests itself in myriad phenomena � Nii!�\n\nAway from thoughts, you see the Buddha,\nBreaking through the dust, you draw out the Sutra.\nThe family Dharma is right here and now: \nWho should establish the [facilities] of the gate at all?\nThe moon follows the boat, flowing into the river of silken purity,\nThe spring comes with the grass, pervading the [fresh] green in the burnt field.\nSwept away? Not swept away? � Listen with utmost care!\nThe three paths are desolate, yet one was able to return;\nThe old pines and chrysanthemums are still balmy and fragrant."
    },
