    "text": {
      "en": "If you move, you bury your body ten thousand feet deep;\nIf you don�t move, roots grow right at your very place.\nEven if you throw away both and cast off the middle,\nYou must buy some straw sandals and set out on a pilgrimage, \nIn order to truly attain it.\n\nT�zan instructed the assembly and said, �At the beginning of autumn and the end of summer, you, brothers, are departing east and west.  But you should go directly to the place of no grass over ten thousand miles.�  And again he said, �How will you go to the place of no grass over ten thousand miles?�  \nSekis� said, �When you go out of the gate, there is grass!�  \nTaiy� said, �I would say:  Even if you don't go out of the gate, grass is abundant everywhere.'�\n\nGrass all over � \nInside the gate, outside the gate � you see it yourself.\nIt is easy to set your foot out of the jungle of thorns;\nIt is difficult to turn out of the luminous screens in the night.\nLook, look!  How much is there?\nFor a while you follow the old tree and become cold and thin as well;\n[Now] you are about to go after the spring wind and to enter the burnt fields."
