    },
    "text": {
      "en": "He has attained the great Samadhi of freely carrying out all godly deeds, \nHe understands the mystic utterances of all living beings [as well as how to maintain them],\nHe turns around Bokush��s �giant drill of the Shin Era�, \nHe plays with the poisonous snake of the southern mountain of Mt. Sepp�:\nDo you know this person?\n\nGreat Master Unmon said, ��Within heaven and earth, in the midst of the universe, there is one treasure hidden in a body.�  You take up the lantern and go to the Buddha Hall; you take the temple gate and put it on the lantern.�\n\nRolling up all the reverberations, disliking fancy things �\nReturning [to oneself], where is one�s life after all?\nThe woodcutter with the rotten axe-handle seems to find no path [back home];\nIn the pot in the cassia tree, as directed by Mr. Pot, a mysterious house is found.\nThe night water with gold ripples reflects the moon;\nThe autumn wind blowing, the snow embraces reed flowers.\nThe cold fish are on the bottom, swallowing no baits; \nLosing interest, one turns the boat homeward with a pure song."
